message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ledgermind: AI-assisted double-entry accounting on Beancount with human review and audit trail"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-22
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/amirani8137/ledgermind"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mirani
    given-names: Ajay Parmanand
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-6208-4755"
  - family-names: Menghani
    given-names: Deepa
keywords:
  - accounting
  - double-entry bookkeeping
  - Beancount
  - transaction categorization
  - human-in-the-loop AI
  - audit trail
abstract: >-
  ledgermind converts bank, credit card, loan and brokerage statements into
  balanced Beancount double-entry ledgers. AI suggests transaction categories
  but never posts directly: low-confidence results go to a human review queue,
  every batch is validated before it is accepted, invalid batches are
  quarantined, and each entry records the statement file and line it came from.
